<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 17 May, from 1521 to 1973.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Duke of Buckingham is executed for treason</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Edward <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stafford">Stafford</a>, Duke of Buckingham, was beheaded on Tower Hill after a trial for allegedly plotting against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>. His fall showed how dangerous royal blood had become under the Tudors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mississippi-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1673">1673 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">353 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jolliet and Marquette set out to explore the Mississippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-jolliet">Louis Jolliet</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuit</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jacques-marquette">Jacques Marquette</a> left St Ignace with five companions in two canoes. They travelled down the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkansas">Arkansas</a> River, mapping it for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1792">1792 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">234 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Brokers sign the Buttonwood Agreement on Wall Street</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Twenty-four brokers agreed to trade securities among themselves at a fixed commission. Their pact, traditionally signed under a buttonwood tree, is the origin of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a> Stock Exchange.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1954">1954 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">72 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Supreme Court strikes down school segregation</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In Brown v. Board of Education the US Supreme Court ruled unanimously that racially segregated public schools were unconstitutional, overturning the 'separate but equal' doctrine in education.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Senate Watergate hearings open on television</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate committee began televised hearings into the Watergate break-in and cover-up. Testimony revealed the White House taping system, which led to Nixon's resignation in August 1974.</p></div></li></ol>
